[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/HBoxContainer/Objective Panel"]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[b]Objective: Learn OR[/b]
The [color=cyan]OR[/color] block is a \"Collector\". It takes all the colors from [b]both[/b] inputs and adds them together.

Your goal: Combine [color=red]Red[/color] and [color=blue]Blue[/color]!

[b]Java Equivalent:[/b]
In Java, this is the [b]`|`[/b] (OR) operator.

We can think of colors as numbers:
[color=gray]// 100 in binary[/color]
[code]int RED   = 4;[/code]
[color=gray]// 001 in binary[/color]
[code]int BLUE  = 1;[/code]

When we combine them with [b]`|`[/b]:
[code]int RESULT = 4 | 1;[/code]
The result is [b]5[/b]!

[b]Why 5?[/b]
   [color=red]100[/color] (Red)
[color=cyan]OR[/color] [color=blue]001[/color] (Blue)
----------
   [b]101[/b] (Red AND Blue are on!)

[code]101[/code] in binary is [b]5[/b]. You collected both!"

